        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(discord): refresh member roles after join or leave",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Discord users who leave or rejoin a guild can retain stale cached member roles for up to 30 seconds. During that interval, role-based Discord voice admission can evaluate the user's previous membership state.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDiscord now invalidates cached member and user entities for `GUILD_MEMBER_ADD` and `GUILD_MEMBER_REMOVE`, matching the existing `GUILD_MEMBER_UPDATE` behavior. The change stays inside the Discord plugin cache boundary and does not add configuration, compatibility shims, or per-event allocations.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDiscord role changes caused by leaving or joining a guild are reflected on the next member lookup instead of waiting for the REST cache TTL. This prevents removed or rejoined users from being authorized with stale role data.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent `upstream/main` at `923d92bdd0e3ddb978ab566efe29a737dc204edf`, using a direct source import of `DiscordEntityCache`:\n\n```text\nGUILD_MEMBER_ADD: before=2 after=2 STALE\nGUILD_MEMBER_REMOVE: before=2 after=2 STALE\nGUILD_MEMBER_UPDATE: before=2 after=4 PASS\n```\n\nExact PR head `2c2f32886853a9ef604098d7238c0a8b8768ab2b`, using the same direct source probe:\n\n```text\nGUILD_MEMBER_ADD: before=2 after=4 PASS\nGUILD_MEMBER_REMOVE: before=2 after=4 PASS\nGUILD_MEMBER_UPDATE: before=2 after=4 PASS\nexact_head=2c2f32886853a9ef604098d7238c0a8b8768ab2b\n```\n\nFocused regression test:\n\n```text\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/discord/src/internal/entity-cache.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\nTests       7 passed (7)\n```\n\nAdditional checks:\n\n```text\n$ ./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/discord/src/internal/entity-cache.ts extensions/discord/src/internal/entity-cache.test.ts\nAll matched files use the correct format.\n\n$ git diff --check\n# no output\n```\n\nFresh autoreview was attempted against the uncommitted exact patch, but the review engine failed before producing findings because the Responses WebSocket returned HTTP 403. No autoreview-clean claim is made.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the complete cache invalidation path, Gateway dispatch caller, and Discord voice role authorization consumer, and I understand the change.\n",
